            <div class="help-section">
              <h4><i class="app-icon" data-lucide="layers"></i> Multi-Selection & Scene Tree</h4>
              <p style="font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5">
                • <strong>Unified Multi-Transform:</strong> When multiple meshes are selected, a bounding proxy gizmo moves, rotates, and scales all items together with undo/redo support.<br />
                • <strong>Outliner Tree Selection:</strong> Click any mesh in the Scene Outliner to select it. Use <span class="shortcut-tag" style="font-size:10px">Cmd/Ctrl+Click</span> to toggle multi-selection or <span class="shortcut-tag" style="font-size:10px">Shift+Click</span> for range selection.<br />
                • <strong>Gizmo Switching:</strong> Switch gizmos (Move, Rotate, Scale, Bounds) at any time without losing your current selection.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="help-section">
              <h4><i class="app-icon" data-lucide="sparkles"></i> 3D Modeling & AI Workflow Tips</h4>
              <p style="font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5">
                • <strong>Separate Loose Parts:</strong> AI-generated meshes often merge all pieces into one mesh. Click "Separate" to split disconnected parts into distinct objects.<br />
                • <strong>Merge Meshes:</strong> Combine multiple selected meshes into a single unified object while preserving all material channels.<br />
                • <strong>Center Pivot:</strong> Click "Center Pivot" if gizmos appear offset from the mesh visual geometry.<br />
                • <strong>Pick & Place:</strong> In the Tools menu, choose "Create Mesh" and click on any surface to spawn new primitives precisely in 3D.<br />
                • <strong>Snapping Increments:</strong> Open <strong>Settings</strong> (gear icon in the top-right toolbar) to adjust Move Snap distance (units) and Rotate Snap angle (degrees).
              </p>
            </div>

